# Go AI Agent Guidance

When working with Go projects, AI agents should prefer Go-native tools instead of web search:

- `go doc <package>` — View package documentation from the active module/workspace
- `go doc <package>.<symbol>` or `go doc <package> <symbol>` — View specific function/type documentation
- `go doc "$(go env GOMODCACHE)/<module>@<version>/<package>.<symbol>"` — View docs for a package already present in the module cache when outside a Go module
- `gopls` — Use the Go language server for code analysis, symbols, and navigation

Avoid web search for Go documentation unless the information is not available via `go doc` or `gopls`.
